{
  "title": "People, countries and です",
  "note": "X は Y です means \"X is Y\"; は (read wa) marks the topic. The negative is じゃありません (more formal: ではありません). Put か at the end to ask a question. の links nouns: 私の名前 \"my name\". も replaces は to mean \"also\". Japanese often drops 私 and あなた when the meaning is clear.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Tae Kim's Guide: Introduction to Particles (は, も, が)",
    "u": "https://guidetojapanese.org/learn/grammar/particlesintro"
  },
